.TH zux 1 "2026-08-25" "zux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zux \- mDNS-SD visualizer with force-directed graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zux
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
zux is an mDNS-SD visualizer. It automatically discovers all services advertised
on your local network via multicast DNS service discovery (mDNS-SD), then renders
them as an interactive force-directed graph so you can see at a glance which
services, instances, hosts and addresses are present and how they relate to one
another.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-I , \-\-include\-non\-link\-local\-ipv6
Include non-link-local IPv6 addresses (global and ULA)
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level\ LOG_LEVEL
Set log level [default: info] [possible values: trace, debug, info, warn, error]
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-to\-file
Enable logging to file
.TP
.BI \-d , \-\-disable\-dmabuf\-renderer
Disable dmabuf renderer (Linux only), useful when having rendering issues
.TP
.BI \-e , \-\-disable\-nv\-explicit\-sync
Disable NVIDIA explicit sync even if NVIDIA is not detected (Linux only)
.TP
.BI \-n , \-\-no\-nvidia\-workaround
Disable all NVIDIA workarounds entirely (Linux only)
.TP
.BI \-v , \-\-nvidia\-workaround\-verbose
Print diagnostic notes when applying an NVIDIA workaround (Linux only)
.TP
.BI \-h , \-\-help
Print help
.TP
.BI \-V , \-\-version
Print version
.SH LOGGING
If enabled with --log-to-file, a log file will be created in a platform-specific location:
.nf
Linux: $XDG_DATA_HOME/com.github.hrzlgnm.zux/logs or $HOME/.local/share/com.github.hrzlgnm.zux/logs
macOS: ~/Library/Logs/com.github.hrzlgnm.zux
Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\com.github.hrzlgnm.zux\\logs
.fi
The log file will be named zux.log and will contain log messages with a log-level having at least the level specified by the log-level option.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WEBKIT2GTK_NVIDIA_QUIRK_VERBOSE
Controls diagnostic output of the underlying
.B webkit2gtk\-nvidia\-quirk
crate (Linux only).
Set it to
.B debug
(or
.BR trace ,
.BR verbose ,
or
.B 2 )
to print a full detection summary \(em session type, whether the primary GPU
and NVIDIA driver are in use, the detected compositor, and the chosen
workaround \(em in addition to the per\-workaround note printed by
.B \-v /\-\-nvidia\-workaround\-verbose .
See https://docs.rs/webkit2gtk-nvidia-quirk for the full list of accepted values.
.SH REPORTING ISSUES
Report bugs or issues at https://github.com/hrzlgnm/zux/issues
